        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n7",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available within 24 hours"
      ],
      "reason": "These elements claim to model the positive code-available branch but systematically append an unsourced '(train)' qualifier to every step, distorting the scope."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Otherwise, if 24 hours have passed, you should call a travel agency.",
        "the process will end"
      ],
      "reason": "Drops the explicit '24 hours have passed' time condition from the preceding guard logic and incorrectly wraps a direct process termination into a standalone action step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10",
        "guard:b3->n11",
        "guard:b3->n12",
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a code is available within 24 hours"
      ],
      "reason": "Duplicates the previous logic with an invented '(flight)' suffix. Critically, action:n12 misstates the required action, using 'call travel agency' where the source dictates a different outcome for the unavailable path."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if a code is not available",
        "the process will end as well"
      ],
      "reason": "Repeats the distortion pattern from the train branch, appending '(flight)' and treating a structural process end as a redundant action step."
    }
  ],
